#: src/routes/dan-estimates.tsx
#~ msgid "Accuracy decides the tier, not just whether you passed. On a ladder whose courses ask for 96%, a bare 96% pass on the delta course reads as <0>delta</0>, 97.5% as <1>delta+</1>, 98% and up as <2>delta++</2>, and coming up short at 93.5% still reads as <3>delta--</3>, because nearly clearing a course is worth more than nothing. Anything under that credits nothing at all. Ladders that ask for a different accuracy shift the whole scale with them."
#~ msgstr "准度决定档次，不只是过没过。在课题要求 96% 的段位系统里，delta 课题上刚好 96% 的通过读作 <0>delta</0>，97.5% 读作 <1>delta+</1>，98% 及以上读作 <2>delta++</2>，而 93.5% 差一点没过仍然读作 <3>delta--</3>，因为差一点通关也比什么都没有强。再低就完全不算。要求别的准度的段位系统，整条刻度也跟着平移。"

#: src/routes/dan-estimates.tsx
#~ msgid "Accuracy decides the tier, not just whether you passed. On a ladder whose courses ask for 96%, a bare 96% pass on the delta course reads as <0>delta</0>, 97.5% as <1>delta+</1>, 98% and up as <2>delta++</2>, and coming up short at 94% still reads as <3>delta--</3>, because nearly clearing a course is worth more than nothing. Anything under that credits nothing at all. Ladders that ask for a different accuracy shift the whole scale with them."
#~ msgstr "准度决定档次，不只是过没过。在课题要求 96% 的段位系统里，delta 课题上刚好 96% 的通过读作 <0>delta</0>，97.5% 读作 <1>delta+</1>，98% 及以上读作 <2>delta++</2>，而 94% 差一点没过仍然读作 <3>delta--</3>，因为差一点通关也比什么都没有强。再低就完全不算。要求别的准度的段位系统，整条刻度也跟着平移。"

